    <string name="battery_title">Why alerts can be late</string>
    <string name="battery_why">Android holds back background checks while your phone sleeps, and some phones stop them to save battery. Letting Triage run in the background keeps alerts on time.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_oneplus">On OnePlus phones: open Triage\'s App info, then Battery usage, and turn on Allow background activity.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_samsung">On Samsung phones: open Triage\'s App info, then Battery, and choose Unrestricted. Also check that Triage isn\'t in Sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_xiaomi">On Xiaomi, Redmi and POCO phones: open Triage\'s App info, then Battery saver, choose No restrictions, and turn on Autostart.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_oppo">On Oppo and Realme phones: open Triage\'s App info, then Battery usage, and allow background activity and auto launch.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_vivo">On vivo phones: open Settings, then Battery, then Background power consumption management, and allow Triage.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_huawei">On Huawei and Honor phones: open Settings, then Battery, then App launch, find Triage and switch it to Manage manually with every option on.</string>
    <string name="battery_tip_generic">In the list that opens, choose All apps, find Triage and choose Don\'t optimize (or Unrestricted).</string>
    <string name="battery_open_settings">Open battery settings</string>

